    <title type="link" role="preferences">Text Attributes</title>
  </info>
  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Text attributes
  </title>
  <p>
    Text attributes describe the font, style, alignment, colors, and other formatting associated
    with text. The information available to Orca depends on which attributes the application
    exposes to assistive technologies.
  </p>
  <section id="checking-formatting">
    <title>Checking formatting</title>
    <p>
      Press <keyseq>
        <key>Orca Modifier</key>
        <key>F</key>
      </keyseq>
      to present formatting information for the current character. In Text Attributes
      preferences, you can configure which attributes are spoken and the order in which they are
      presented. Orca omits attributes whose values are treated as defaults. You can customize
      these selections for individual applications.
    </p>
    <p>
      Press the same key combination twice quickly to open a window showing all available
      attributes for that character, including attributes you have not enabled for speech. You
      can read and copy the details. Press <key>Escape</key> to close the window.
    </p>
    <p>
      When flat review is active, these commands use the character at the review location.
      Otherwise, they use the character at the text caret. If no formatting information is
      available, Orca tells you.
    </p>
    <section id="settings-checking-formatting">
      <title>Settings</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Text Attributes</gui> category.
      </p>
      <p>
        The list contains one row for each text attribute. Use the presentation mode on a row to
        choose whether Orca speaks the attribute, marks it in braille, does both, or does
        neither. Use the row menu or drag handle to change the order in which attributes are
        presented. The speech choices apply when you request the current character's formatting;
        they do not filter automatic formatting-change announcements.
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Text Attributes</gui>: Lists text
            attributes and lets you choose whether each one is spoken, marked in braille, both,
            or neither. Choices: None, Speak, Mark in braille, Speak and mark.
          </p>
          <list>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>None</gui>: Does not present the
                attribute.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Speak</gui>: Speaks the attribute.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Mark in braille</gui>: Marks the
                attribute in braille.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Speak and mark</gui>: Speaks the
                attribute and marks it in braille.
              </p>
            </item>
          </list>
          <list>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Reorder</gui>: Moves the selected
                text attribute earlier or later in the presentation order.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Move to top</gui>: Moves the selected
                text attribute to the top of the list.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Move up one</gui>: Moves the selected
                text attribute up one position.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Move down one</gui>: Moves the selected
                text attribute down one position.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Move to bottom</gui>: Moves the selected
                text attribute to the bottom of the list.
              </p>
            </item>
          </list>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
    <section id="commands-checking-formatting">
      <title>Commands</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Object details</gui> group.
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Present character formatting</gui>
            <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
