  <section id="automatic-announcements">
    <title>Automatic announcements</title>
    <p>
      Orca can announce formatting changes, such as bold or italic, as you move through text. In
      Speech preferences, open Verbosity and set Text attribute changes to Off, Editable text
      only, or Always. Say All has a separate Text attribute changes setting for continuous
      reading.
    </p>
    <p>
      Automatic announcements are independent of the attribute list used by the explicit
      formatting command.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Cycle to the next text attribute change mode command switches among these announcement
      modes for the current session.
    </p>
    <p>
      Applications can also expose spelling and grammar errors as text attributes, often
      corresponding to a squiggly underline on screen. Orca can announce these errors when you
      move into the affected text or when the application marks a word as misspelled while you
      type.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Misspelled-word indicator setting in Speech preferences controls these error
      announcements and is enabled by default. These announcements do not require key echo or
      word echo to be enabled.
    </p>
    <section id="commands-automatic-announcements">
      <title>Commands</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Speech and verbosity</gui> group.
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Cycle to the next text attribute change mode</gui>
            Unbound by default.
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
