  <section id="braille-indicators">
    <title>Braille indicators</title>
    <p>
      In Text Attributes preferences, you can configure which attributes are marked in braille,
      independently of which ones are spoken. Enable braille marking for the mistake attribute
      to mark spelling and grammar errors.
    </p>
    <p>
      In Braille preferences, open Display Settings and configure the Text Attributes indicator.
      These dots act like underlining on the braille display. The same indicator is used for all
      attributes you have enabled for braille; it shows where an attribute is present, rather
      than which attribute it is. If the indicator is set to None, no attribute markers are
      shown.
    </p>
    <p>
      See also:
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <link xref="features_braille_display_settings#settings-display-settings">Display Settings preferences</link>: Configure
          wrapping, contraction, and the dots used to mark text in braille.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
